<!-- ======================================================= COVER -->
<section class="page">
  <div class="small">NESFIC 2026 · Challenge NESFIC-D-35 · Agriculture Department, Government of Assam</div>
  <h1 style="margin-top:6mm">Proof of Work<br><span style="font-size:15pt;color:var(--ink)">Bazar Sanket (<span class="as">বজাৰ সংকেত</span>): price intelligence and forecasting for Assam farmers</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">A working prototype built on real public market data: it measures the data problem, forecasts prices one to four weeks ahead with an honest out-of-sample test, turns forecasts into Hold / Sell / Store advice, and shows how farmers, Extension Assistants and AMIU would use it.</p>
  <p class="small">Applicant: Arijit Gogoi (individual applicant) · Prepared ${today} · Data retrieved ${retrieved}</p>

  <div class="kpis">
    <div class="kpi"><b>${rows_total}</b><span>Agmarknet price records used (${assam_rows} for Assam since ${assam_first_year})</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>${weeks_empty_pct}%</b><span>of weeks since ${assam_first_year} with no Assam price at all in the public record</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>${all_mape_model}%</b><span>forecast error (MAPE, 1–4 weeks, ${n_series_assam} Assam series, 12 months out of sample); no-change benchmark ${all_mape_naive}%</span></div>
    <div class="kpi"><b>${S3_pooled}%</b><span>error forecasting Assam with <i>no</i> Assam history, learning only from neighbouring States (no-change: ${S3_naive}%)</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="box">
    <b>What this document shows</b>
    <ul>
      <li><b>The problem, measured</b> (Section A): gaps, renamed markets and patchy reporting in the public Assam record.</li>
      <li><b>User journey and mock-ups</b> (Sections B–C): Assamese and English SMS, WhatsApp card and voice script; Extension Assistant dashboard; AMIU review console; crop-planning card. All mock-ups show real prototype outputs for the week of ${end_week}.</li>
      <li><b>How the prototype works</b> (Section D) and <b>how well it works</b> (Sections E–H): a rolling-origin backtest against benchmarks and other methods (Holt-Winters, volatility pricing, LightGBM), repeated on all ${ext_k} Assam commodities with good data, a stress test of incomplete data, a backtest of the Hold / Sell / Store rule and an out-of-sample check of the season-ahead outlook.</li>
      <li><b>Target architecture, limitations and next steps</b> (Sections I–J).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small" style="margin:0">Labels used throughout: <span class="tag built">BUILT + TESTED</span> working code run on real data · <span class="tag mock">MOCK-UP</span> design shown with real prototype numbers, not yet deployed · <span class="tag plan">PLANNED</span> part of the proposal, not yet built.</p>
