<section class="page" style="margin-top:7mm">
  <h2>H. Season-ahead outlook: does the seasonal pattern hold out of sample? <span class="tag built">BUILT + TESTED</span></h2>
  <p>Crop planning needs a view of prices months ahead. The prototype's first step is the seasonal price profile: how far each month's price typically sits above or below the year's average, pooled across Assam and neighbouring markets. To test it honestly, for each year we estimated the profile only from earlier years and compared it with the actual monthly pattern in Assam markets that year.</p>
  ${table_season}
  <p>${season_reading}</p>
  <p class="small">Planned next steps for the long horizon: add trend and year-level drivers (area sown, rainfall, neighbouring-State prices before sowing) to forecast the level, not just the shape, of harvest-window prices; express outlooks as ranges; and score each season's outlook after harvest.</p>
</section>

