<!-- ======================================================= J -->
<section class="page" style="margin-top:7mm">
  <h2>J. Limitations, assumptions and next steps</h2>
  <h3>Limitations of this prototype (stated plainly)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Only public Agmarknet prices were used. The public dataset has <b>no arrivals</b>; AMIU arrivals data are requested, not assumed.</li>
    <li>The three pilot series were chosen by a coverage rule; all are vegetables in one Guwahati market. Results may differ for storable crops and smaller markets; the pilot will test agreed commodities.</li>
    <li>The test year (${test_start} to ${end_week}) follows a three-month reporting gap at the Agmarknet 2.0 cut-over, which makes early test weeks harder than usual.</li>
    <li>Decision-rule parameters are illustrative; the decision backtest uses modal market prices, not prices actually received by farmers.</li>
    <li>The season-ahead component forecasts the seasonal shape, not yet the price level.</li>
    <li>Assamese text is a draft translation pending native-speaker review.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Next steps (see proposal timeline)</h3>
  <ol class="small">
    <li>Agree pilot commodities, markets and districts with the department; request AMIU historical data and feed.</li>
    <li>Retrain and re-test on AMIU data, adding arrivals; add storable crops (e.g. potato, mustard, paddy).</li>
    <li>Calibrate decision rules with AAU; co-design and test Assamese messages with AEAs and farmers.</li>
    <li>Build review console, dashboard and channels; run 6–8 weeks in shadow mode; validation-readiness review at month 6.</li>
    <li>Pilot for one season with a public scorecard.</li>
  </ol>
  <h3>Data sources and licence</h3>
  <p class="small">Agmarknet daily mandi prices (Directorate of Marketing &amp; Inspection, Ministry of Agriculture &amp; Farmers Welfare), via the data.gov.in Open Government Data API, resource 35985678-0d79-46b4-9ed6-6f13308a1d24 "Variety-wise Daily Market Prices Data of Commodity", Government Open Data License – India. Retrieved ${retrieved}; ${rows_total} records. References: Montero-Manso, P. &amp; Hyndman, R. J. (2021), Principles and algorithms for forecasting groups of time series: Locality and globality, International Journal of Forecasting 37(4); Makridakis, S., Spiliotis, E. &amp; Assimakopoulos, V. (2022), M5 accuracy competition: Results, findings, and conclusions, International Journal of Forecasting 38(4).</p>
</section>

